<title>CHINA: China's January cereal imports detailed.</title>
<headline>China's January cereal imports detailed.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following table shows the wheat, barley, corn and rice import figures of up to five major Chinese import offices as well as the country of origin during January 1997.</p>
<p>Details were provided by the General Administration of Customs of China.</p>
<p>Figures are in tonnes. Percentages represent the share of the total market. Percentages may not add up to 100 percent as details of some smaller import regions and supplying countries have not been included.</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p> Jan imports:   163,898</p>
<p>  CUSTOMS	     Jan	    Pct</p>
<p>    Fuzhou	 15,459	    9.4</p>
<p>    Shanghai	    0	    0.0</p>
<p>    Huangpu	31,500	   19.2</p>
<p>    Nanning	89,250	   54.5</p>
<p>Jiulong</p>
<p>     (Shenzhen)  27,688	   16.7</p>
<p>ORIGINS</p>
<p>    Canada	126,000	   76.9</p>
<p>    U.S.	   31,857	   19.4</p>
<p>    Australia     6,039	    3.7</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p> Jan imports:   176,488</p>
<p>  CUSTOMS	     Jan	    Pct</p>
<p>    Nanjing	52,500	   29.7</p>
<p>    Shanghai     44,696	   25.3</p>
<p>    Tianjin	26,200	   14.8</p>
<p>    Huangpu	26,250	   14.9</p>
<p>    Ningbo	 26,842	   15.2</p>
<p>ORIGINS</p>
<p>    Spain	  26,842	   15.2</p>
<p>    Australia    26,200	   10.6</p>
<p>    Canada	123,446	   69.9</p>
<p>RICE</p>
<p> Jan imports:   63,873</p>
<p>  CUSTOMS	    Jan	    Pct</p>
<p>    Huangpu     27,350	   42.8</p>
<p>    Jiulong     24,049	   37.7</p>
<p>(Shenzhen)</p>
<p>    Guangzhou	181	    0.2</p>
<p>    Wuhan	     35	    0.05</p>
<p>    Xiamen	 4,399	    6.9</p>
<p>ORIGINS</p>
<p>    Thailand    63,462	   99.3</p>
<p>    U.S.		54	    0.08</p>
